{"id":"texture_scatter","compound_name":"Graphs::Texture::texture_scatter","source_path":"texture_scatter/texture_scatter.json","category":"Texture","author":"Autodesk","description":"This graph illustrates the use of read_texture to drive a scatter density and output color.","documentation_file":"texture_scatter_docs_ENU.md","documentation":"## texture_scatter\n\n### What it does\n\nThis graph illustrates the use of read_texture to drive a scatter density.  Because the texture compound outputs a Bifrost object, the output can be plugged into an interpreted auto port and can be assigned as a diagnostic texture or scatter weights for example.\n\n### Inputs and outputs\n\nThe image to read is one that is included with the default Maya installation. It can be set to any image. The output is a Bifrost Object.\nThe output is this graph is scattered points colored by the input image.\n\n### How it works\n\n- The `read_texture` node is used to read a texture from a file.\n\n- The `file_path` input recognises some tokens for path resolution as well as supporting environment variables and frame numbers in the filename.  Please see the compound info tab for more details.\n\n- The compound supports `file_color_space` input as a string.  If left as the default empty string the node will attempt to determine the colorspace automatically using OpenColorIO.  Use \"raw\" to bypass any colorspace conversion.","library_dependencies":{"Amino":"2.15.0.9","bif":"2.15.0.9","file":"2.15.0.9","scatter":"2.15.0.9"},"graph_ports":[],"terminal_states":[{"name":"Core::Graph::terminal::final","enabled":"true"},{"name":"Core::Graph::terminal::diagnostic","enabled":"true"}],"counts":{"nodes":9,"connections":10,"values":50,"compounds":1},"node_types":{"Modeling::Points::scatter_points":1,"File::Image::read_texture":1,"Modeling::Primitive::create_mesh_plane":1,"Core::String::expand_env_vars":1,"Rendering::Materials::standard_surface_mat":1,"Rendering::Materials::set_geo_property_reference":1,"Diagnostic::Display::assign_diagnostic_material":1,"Rendering::Materials::assign_material":1,"Core::Graph::terminal":1},"edge_type_pairs":{"Modeling::Primitive::create_mesh_plane -> Modeling::Points::scatter_points":1,"Rendering::Materials::standard_surface_mat -> Rendering::Materials::set_geo_property_reference":1,"Rendering::Materials::set_geo_property_reference -> Rendering::Materials::assign_material":1,"Diagnostic::Display::assign_diagnostic_material -> Rendering::Materials::assign_material":1,"Diagnostic::Display::assign_diagnostic_material -> Core::Graph::terminal":1,"Rendering::Materials::assign_material -> Core::Graph::terminal":1,"Modeling::Points::scatter_points -> Diagnostic::Display::assign_diagnostic_material":1,"File::Image::read_texture -> Diagnostic::Display::assign_diagnostic_material":1,"File::Image::read_texture -> Modeling::Points::scatter_points":1,"Core::String::expand_env_vars -> File::Image::read_texture":1},"nodes":[{"path":"root","name":"scatter_points","type":"Modeling::Points::scatter_points"},{"path":"root","name":"read_texture","type":"File::Image::read_texture","terminal_states":[{"name":"Core::Graph::terminal::diagnostic","enabled":"false"}]},{"path":"root","name":"create_mesh_plane","type":"Modeling::Primitive::create_mesh_plane"},{"path":"root","name":"expand_env_vars1","type":"Core::String::expand_env_vars"},{"path":"root","name":"standard_surface_mat","type":"Rendering::Materials::standard_surface_mat"},{"path":"root","name":"set_geo_property_reference","type":"Rendering::Materials::set_geo_property_reference"},{"path":"root","name":"assign_diagnostic_material1","type":"Diagnostic::Display::assign_diagnostic_material"},{"path":"root","name":"assign_material","type":"Rendering::Materials::assign_material"},{"path":"root","name":"terminal","type":"Core::Graph::terminal","fan_in_ports":{"final":["out_geometry"],"proxy":[],"diagnostic":["geometry_with_material"]},"terminal_states":[{"name":"Core::Graph::terminal::final","enabled":"true"},